Negative control for the stop that stays in view (`R6-24`).

Drops the scroll off the playhead watcher and nothing else: the rail still finds
the marked stop on every move, still draws done · current · pending, still
scrubs, and still lays out identically — so the only claim that can go red is
the ruled one. The rail and the Scenario sheet's list are two views of the SAME
stops, and a lane wide enough to scroll leaves the current stop off its own
right-hand edge two scenes into a playback: a playhead nobody can see is not a
playhead.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: transport.spec.ts — the `R6-24` scene-rail case (advancing the playhead
brings the marked stop into the lane).

